      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection debate",
          "heading": "Will Greenwood suggests Andy Farrell play Ciaran Frawley at 12",
          "body": "Will Greenwood, the 2003 England World Cup winner, says in his view Andy Farrell should solve the No. 10 debate by picking Ciaran Frawley at inside centre alongside Sam Prendergast. Frawley, who quit Leo Cullen's Leinster earlier this year after being overlooked for the 10 shirt, has started impressively at Connacht, and with Jack Crowley unavailable through injury, he is now seen as a genuine rival at 10. Nearly all of his 15 Test caps have come as a replacement."
        },
