    "463": {
      "date": "2026-10-21",
      "edition": "Wednesday 21 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "League One rules",
          "heading": "Hajime Shoji's League One backtracks on foreign-born player rules after backlash",
          "body": "Japan Rugby League One backtracked on contentious registration rules on 28 August, after legal challenges and a fierce backlash from players and fans. Naturalised players who acquired Japanese citizenship, or applied for it, by May 2025 will now be treated as Japanese-born under the system due in the 2026-27 season. The original proposal would have kept them outside the Japanese category, cutting places for foreign-born players eligible to represent Japan. Managing Executive Director Hajime Shoji said: \"We lacked communication with players who would be adversely affected by the changes.\""
        },
