      "edition": "Wednesday 21 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Form watch",
          "heading": "Steve Hansen credits Beauden Barrett's midfield marshalling for Sydney Bledisloe win",
          "body": "Sir Steve Hansen's view on the Rugby Unity podcast is that Beauden Barrett's work in midfield was a key reason for the Bledisloe Cup win in Sydney: the 35-year-old marshalled Timoci Tavatavanawai and Rieko Ioane, and Hansen says that is something \"you can't buy\". Barrett started both Bledisloe Tests at full-back, and his form has returned after a difficult Super Rugby Pacific campaign and an underwhelming South Africa tour. New Zealand's 43-21 win on Saturday secured the 2-0 series result."
        },
